[00:19.44]1. Our happy God is merciful,
[00:26.72]His mercy not just dutiful.
[00:32.92]He takes delight in kindly deeds
[00:38.48]And freely grants our daily needs.
[00:45.02]Repentant ones can be assured
[00:51.48]Their plea for mercy will be heard.
[01:00.00]Remembering that we are dust,
[01:04.38]He’s merciful and kind and just.
[01:14.54]2. When we have sinned and feel distressed,
[01:43.36]When God’s forgiveness we request,
[01:49.58]Our Lord, Christ Jesus, showed the way
[01:55.34]To ask for mercy when we pray:
[02:01.94]“Forgive our debts, we beg of you,
[02:07.46]As we forgive our debtors too.”
[02:07.50]We then can let resentment go,
[02:20.96]And peace of mind and heart we’ll know.
[02:47.40]3. When gifts of mercy we bestow,
[02:53.86]The giving spirit we should show.
[03:00.06]We give without desiring praise,
[03:06.52]Content with joy our gift conveys.
[03:12.28]Then God, who sees all things we do,
[03:18.44]Will be the One repaying you.
[03:25.72]Yes, happy are the merciful,
[03:31.94]In God’s eyes they are beautiful.
